  <tips>
    <item>
      <position>0</position>
      <data>we need more tips?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>1</position>
      <data>you can change the color of the display through settings?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>2</position>
      <data>you can hide the scrollbars to increase the viewable area through settings?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>3</position>
      <data>you can change the icon size for increased visibility?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>4</position>
      <data>you can toggle the grid on and off by pressing the button in the statusbar?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>5</position>
      <data>the grid size can be changed to match your hoop size through settings?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>6</position>
      <data>the crosshair size is based on a percentage of your screen size? Setting it to 100 may help you visually line things up better.</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>7</position>
      <data>you can pan by pressing the middle mouse button and dragging your mouse across the screen?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>8</position>
      <data>you can open and edit multiple designs simultaneously?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>9</position>
      <data>you that many embroidery machines support the .dst format?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>10</position>
      <data>that you can zoom in and out using your mouse wheel?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>11</position>
      <data>that you can use circular and isometric grids?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>12</position>
      <data>about our command line format converter?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>13</position>
      <data>that you can use the 'DAY' and 'NIGHT' commands to quickly switch the view colors to commonly used white or black?</data>
    </item>
    <item>
      <position>14</position>
      <data>that you can quickly change the background, crosshair and grid colors using the 'RGB' command?"</data>
    </item>
  </tips>
